+  TopAbs_State TestOnRestriction(const gp_Pnt2d& Puv,
+                                 const double    Tol,
+                                 const bool      RecadreOnPeriodic = true) const;
+
+  //! Defect 018. true only if Perform(theP, false) certainly returns OutsideState(). Apart from its
+  //! point-independent start (a new BRepAdaptor_Surface of the face, Initialize(), IsUPeriodic() /
+  //! UPeriod() - BRepTopAdaptor_FClass2d.cxx:541-547 @V8_0_1; the constructor already initialised
+  //! the same face at :99-100, so for a face that got a polygon these cannot throw) Perform() with
+  //! RecadreOnPeriodic = false evaluates nothing but TabClass(1).SiDans(P) (:595-636) and returns
+  //! after one pass (:646-649); SiDans() == -1 gives TopAbs_OUT when TabOrien(1) == 1, else IN.
+  //! Conditions (all needed):
+  //!  - one classifier (one wire) whose orientation is known: TabClass.Length() == 1,
+  //!    TabOrien(1) != -1 (otherwise Perform() goes to BRepClass_FaceClassifier, :639-644);
+  //!  - that CSLib_Class2d has points (CSLib_Class2d.cxx:58-62 @V8_0_1: umax > umin, vmax > vmin,
+  //!    >= 3 points), all finite;
+  //!  - theP, in the normalized coordinates SiDans() computes (transformToNormalized of the box
+  //!    handed to CSLib_Class2d, which includes (0,0): BRepTopAdaptor_FClass2d.cxx:106-107), lies
+  //!    outside the box of the stored polygon enlarged by the normalized tolerances myTolU/myTolV
+  //!    SiDans() uses, by a margin of 1e-9 relative.
+  //! Then SiDans() (CSLib_Class2d.cxx:141-187) either returns -1 at its quick rejection test, or
+  //! internalSiDansOuOn() (:279-340) finds no vertex within (myTolU, myTolV), no edge with theP's x
+  //! strictly inside its x range and |dy| <= myTolV (the interpolated y stays within the edge's y
+  //! range up to a few ulps, far below the margin; the PConfusion guard of 8.0.1 only removes such
+  //! tests), and an even ray parity (no sign change of y - Py when Py is below or above the
+  //! polygon; every sign change counts, and a closed polygon has an even number of them, when Px is
+  //! left of it; none counts when Px is right of it) - so Result_Outside. The four corner points
+  //! (Px +- myTolU, Py +- myTolV) stay on the same side, so internalSiDans() (:234-275) gives the
+  //! same parity 0 and SiDans() returns -1.
+  bool IsFarOutside(const gp_Pnt2d& theP) const
+  {
+    if (TabClass.Length() != 1 || TabOrien(1) == -1 || !myPolyOk)
